  "id": "extensive_game.perfect_information.subgame_perfect_equilibrium",
  "title": "Subgame-Perfect Equilibrium In Perfect-Information Games",
  "kind": "definition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "extensive_game/perfect_information/extensive_game_perfect_information_subgame_perfect_equilibrium.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Subgame-Perfect Equilibrium In Perfect-Information Games</h1>\n<p>A strategy profile $\\sigma$ is subgame-perfect if for every position $p$, the\ncontinuation strategy profile $\\sigma[p]$ induced by $\\sigma$ is a Nash equilibrium\nof the subgame $G[p]$.</p>\n<p>This strengthens Nash equilibrium by requiring optimality after every possible\nhistory, including histories not reached by the equilibrium play.</p>",
